# runloop_msg_queue_push() defers an off-main caller before touching
# anything: the worker's message waits under the message queue lock
# for the main thread's iterate to replay it. Its widget, font,
# accessibility and settings work therefore happens on the main
# thread for every caller.
@boundary runloop_msg_queue_push

# The shader backends' per-frame sensor uniforms: the read side of a
# seqlock whose only writer is input_driver_poll() on the main thread
# (nine floats published as bits behind sensor_snap_seq). The getter
# call inside the helper is how it reaches the atomics, not a live
# state read.
input_driver_read_sensor_snapshot|input_state_get_ptr
# Release-store of the atomic shader-demand latch (shader_uses_sensors),
# read with acquire by the poll's demand check. A latch write, not a
# state read.
input_driver_set_shader_uses_sensors|input_state_get_ptr
